+- id: AUG-173
+  title: 'AUG-173: the AUG-130 gate-mode case is hermetic to a docs-only HEAD'
+  criteria:
+  - 'The AUG-130 probe forces the full gate so a docs-only HEAD cannot take the doc-only
+    fast path. PROOF: `grep -c "AUGER_GATE_INNER=1 GATE_FULL=1" tests/test_gate_mode.sh`
+    prints 1. FAILIF: that count is 0 or greater than 1.'
+  - 'The gate-mode case passes at this head and prints its own verdict line. PROOF:
+    `bash tests/test_gate_mode.sh` exits 0 and its output contains "AUG-130 skipped-arm
+    policy: PASS". FAILIF: a non-zero exit, or that line absent from the output.'
+  - 'GATE_FULL is still the documented override that defeats the doc-only shortcut,
+    and the shortcut still exists. PROOF: `grep -c "GATE_FULL" tests/gate.sh` prints
+    2 and `grep -c "doc-only fast path" tests/gate.sh` prints 5. FAILIF: either count
+    drops, meaning the override was removed or the fast path deleted instead of bypassed.'
+  - 'No weakening of the AUG-130 skipped-arm policy. PROOF: `grep -c "env -u AUGER_ALLOW_SKIPPED_ARMS"
+    tests/test_gate_mode.sh` prints 1, `grep -c "GATE PASS (DEGRADED)" tests/test_gate_mode.sh`
+    prints 1, and `git diff c461056..HEAD -- tests/gate.sh` prints nothing. FAILIF:
+    the strict leg sets the escape, the DEGRADED assertion disappears, or tests/gate.sh
+    changed in this branch.'
+  - 'The red-to-green delta is committed as evidence, not asserted in prose. PROOF:
+    `grep -c "AUG-130: gate exited 0" evidence/AUG-173/01-prefix-red-docsonly.txt`
+    prints 1, `grep -c "AUG-130 skipped-arm policy: PASS" evidence/AUG-173/02-postfix-green-docsonly.txt`
+    prints 1, and `grep -c "rc=1" evidence/AUG-173/04-nonvacuity.txt` prints 1. FAILIF:
+    any of the three greps prints 0.'
